I've learned that each of these Pokémon
statues is actually a real Pokémon!{VAR BE01}
It's called Darmanitan. It's sleeping,
so it's become like a stone.{VAR BE01}

When I quickly measured how long
they've existed...{VAR BE01}
It was amazing! Around 2,500 years!
Seems like they went to sleep that{VAR BE00}
long ago.{VAR BE01}
That means they've been here since
before this place was in ruins, when{VAR BE00}
the Relic Castle was flourishing.{VAR BE01}
Perhaps they were guarding the city.{VAR BE01}

These Pokémon...{VAR BE01}
They are either in a state of hibernation
or meditation, so if you wake them, they{VAR BE00}
will become active once again.{VAR BE01}
And the item that wakes up Darmanitan is
actually...this RageCandyBar!{VAR BE01}
That's why I will share one with you,
too, {VAR 0100 0000}!{VAR BE01}

Well, I'm headed back to the
Pokémon Research Lab.{VAR BE00}
Be seeing you!{VAR BE01}

The ancient Pokémon statue responded to
the RageCandyBar.{VAR BE01}
The Pokémon was a sleeping Darmanitan!{VAR BE01}
The awakened Darmanitan attacked!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: That's the entrance to the
Relic Castle.{VAR BE01}
You're impressive, {VAR 0100 0000},
making it here before I did.{VAR BE01}

Dealing with the Desert Resort's Pokémon
took longer than I would've thought.{VAR BE01}
I only made it all the way out here
thanks to my Pokémon.{VAR BE01}

Alder: What could that guy called
N possibly want?{VAR BE01}
Could he be trying to prove he is
right by winning the battle of the{VAR BE00}
two dragons?{VAR BE01}

Alder: I could hear Professor Juniper's
voice from clear over here!{VAR BE00}
Seems like something big is happening.{VAR BE01}
I wonder what is waiting at the museum
in Nacrene City.{VAR BE00}
I'll go on ahead!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: I'll look around here once more.{VAR BE01}
I don't want to believe what
that Ghetsis says...{VAR BE01}
You should head for the
Nacrene City Museum.

You're the first person to come
clear out here to talk to me!{VAR BE01}
I'm so moved!
So, I'll give you this!{VAR BE01}

According to what I've heard, that
Relic Castle is the ruins of a city built{VAR BE00}
by the hero of old and the dragon{VAR BE00}
Pokémon that accompanied the hero.
